            <ArticleTitle>Role of testosterone on pain threshold in rats.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain thresholds were recorded in rats by progressive increase in electrical stimulation to induce tail withdrawal, vocalisation and vocalisation after discharge. It was observed that castration resulted in significant reduction of pain threshold which however returned to normal level on substitution with testosterone therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
